    },
    {
      "@id": "https://www.cosmos.studio/#website",
      "@type": "WebSite",
      "alternateName": "Cosmos",
      "name": "Cosmos Studio",
      "publisher": {
        "@id": "https://www.cosmos.studio/#organization"
      },
      "url": "https://www.cosmos.studio/"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://www.cosmos.studio/#founder",
      "@type": "Person",
      "image": "https://www.cosmos.studio/assets/img/illia-kulbachnyi-ceo-1600.webp",
      "jobTitle": "Founder & CEO",
      "name": "Illia Kulbachnyi",
      "worksFor": {
        "@id": "https://www.cosmos.studio/#organization"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://www.cosmos.studio/#faq",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A UI/UX design studio designs how a digital product works and looks: research, user flows, interface design, and a design system. Cosmos Studio also builds the front end in React and Next.js, so the same team takes your product from the first customer interview to working code."
          },
          "name": "What does a UI/UX design studio do?"
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Projects start at $5,000, with hourly rates from $50. Specialized senior roles, such as AWS cloud architects, can cost up to $170 per hour. After the discovery call, you get a free, non-binding estimate based on the confirmed scope. For a quick range, try our project cost calculator."
          },
          "name": "How much does UI/UX design cost?"
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A typical project takes 2–6 weeks. A landing page takes 1–2 weeks, a brand identity 1–3 weeks, a multi-page CMS website 2–4 weeks, MVP app design 3–4 weeks (4–8 weeks with front-end development), and a UX audit 1–2 weeks. Larger products are delivered in stages, so your developers can start before the whole design is finished."
          },
          "name": "How long does a project take?"
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Book a discovery call. We learn about your product, customers, and goals, and you can ask for an NDA from the first call. Then we agree on scope, deliverables, and price before any work starts."
          },
          "name": "How do we start working together?"
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Because design built on guesses is expensive to fix later. If you already know your customers' needs, we go straight to product hypotheses. If not, we run customer interviews using The Mom Test method, or give you the questions to ask your customers."
          },
          "name": "Why do you start with research?"
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "You see the first results within a week of kickoff. Designs and staging builds are reviewed every week, and nothing moves to the next stage without your sign-off. Day-to-day questions go through Slack or WhatsApp. The team works 10:00–18:00 Kyiv time, which overlaps with US East Coast mornings."
          },
          "name": "What does working with you look like week to week?"
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A dedicated senior team: a product or UI/UX designer and a project manager as your single point of contact. Our design director Alex Chaika reviews every deliverable, and founder Illia Kulbachnyi joins reviews of key stages."
          },
          "name": "Who will work on my project?"
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. We build production front ends in React, Next.js, and TypeScript, and websites on Webflow, WordPress, or custom code. Backend, mobile apps, and cloud are delivered by our vetted senior engineering partners under the same contract."
          },
          "name": "Do you also develop the product?"
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Our designers can join your sprints as an embedded design team, or hand off a design system and code to your developers."
          },
          "name": "Can you work with our in-house team?"
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Defense and military tech, SaaS, AI products, EdTech, MedTech and healthcare, Web3, gaming, B2B and IT services, hospitality, health and wellness, and nonprofits."
          },
          "name": "Which industries do you work with?"
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Every project can operate under an NDA from the first call."
          },
          "name": "Can you work under an NDA?"
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. We share client contacts for references on request. You can also read 21 verified reviews on our Clutch profile and contact the reviewers there."
          },
          "name": "Can we talk to your past clients?"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
